From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:29:15 +0200
Subject: media: hm5065: Make every raw size reachable

The raw sizes are the readout's own, and set_fmt picked between them
with hm5065_get_max_binning(), which asks for the most binning that fits
strictly inside the request. That is the right question for the scaled
path and the wrong one here: asking for exactly 1296x972 returned
2592x1944, and asking for exactly 648x486 returned 1296x972, so two of
the three sizes enum_frame_size() advertises could not be selected by
asking for them.

Round the request up to a readout size instead.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c | 17 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
@@ -1967,8 +1967,21 @@ static int hm5065_set_fmt(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	 * of the processing being bypassed.
 	 */
 	if (hm5065_format_is_raw(pixfmt)) {
-		unsigned int bin = hm5065_get_max_binning(mf->width,
-							  mf->height);
+		unsigned int bin = 1;
+
+		/*
+		 * Round the request up to a readout size rather than picking
+		 * the most binning that fits strictly inside it, which is what
+		 * hm5065_get_max_binning() is for and which would make two of
+		 * the three sizes enum_frame_size() offers unreachable: asking
+		 * for exactly 1296x972 would return the full 2592x1944.
+		 */
+		if (mf->width <= HM5065_SENSOR_WIDTH / 4 &&
+		    mf->height <= HM5065_SENSOR_HEIGHT / 4)
+			bin = 4;
+		else if (mf->width <= HM5065_SENSOR_WIDTH / 2 &&
+			 mf->height <= HM5065_SENSOR_HEIGHT / 2)
+			bin = 2;
 
 		mf->width = HM5065_SENSOR_WIDTH / bin;
 		mf->height = HM5065_SENSOR_HEIGHT / bin;
-- 
